um", "notes": ["Open seat: Andy Barr (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kentucky's 6th district is an open seat after Andy Barr left to run for Senate, removing the incumbent advantage that has cushioned Republicans here. The district leans Republican by about seven points, but the 2026 environment and a competitive Democratic nominee have narrowed the gap. Zach Dembo has matched Ralph Alvarado in fundraising, and Democratic-sponsored polls from late September show him narrowly ahead.\n\nMost professional raters now call the race Lean Republican, though a few still say Likely R and one calls it a Tossup. Prediction markets continue to favor Alvarado by a wide margin. The forecast lands just on the Republican side, with meaningful uncertainty given thin and partisan polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.2515, "margin": -3.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.296, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2877, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2982, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.223, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2389, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2735, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2956, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2849, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.3514, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.3215, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3486, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3422, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3273, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3239, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.2888, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.3735, "margin": -2.0}]}